-DATASET CSV empty
--
# Hermetic D3 gate: UNION / UNION ALL. Runs under `cargo test` (no dataset).
# tinysnb corpus-exact cases live in tests/p1/union.test.

-CASE UnionPositive
-STATEMENT CREATE NODE TABLE N(id INT64, name STRING, PRIMARY KEY(id))
---- ok
-STATEMENT CREATE (:N {id:1, name:'a'})
---- ok
-STATEMENT CREATE (:N {id:2, name:'b'})
---- ok
-STATEMENT CREATE (:N {id:3, name:'a'})
---- ok
# UNION ALL concatenates and keeps duplicates.
-STATEMENT MATCH (n:N) RETURN n.name UNION ALL MATCH (m:N) RETURN m.name
---- 6
a
a
a
a
b
b
# UNION deduplicates over all columns.
-STATEMENT MATCH (n:N) RETURN n.name UNION MATCH (m:N) RETURN m.name
---- 2
a
b
# Chained UNION ALL (3 operands, left-associative), mixing a MATCH and an UNWIND.
-STATEMENT MATCH (n:N) RETURN n.id UNION ALL MATCH (m:N) RETURN m.id UNION ALL UNWIND [99] AS x RETURN x
---- 7
1
1
2
2
3
3
99
# UNION over literal operands deduplicates.
-STATEMENT RETURN 1 AS x UNION RETURN 2 AS x UNION RETURN 1 AS x
---- 2
1
2
# Multi-column UNION ALL.
-STATEMENT MATCH (n:N) RETURN n.id, n.name UNION ALL MATCH (m:N) WHERE m.name='a' RETURN m.id, m.name
---- 5
1|a
1|a
2|b
3|a
3|a
# Aggregates in each operand.
-STATEMENT MATCH (n:N) RETURN count(*) AS c UNION ALL MATCH (n:N) WHERE n.name='a' RETURN count(*) AS c
---- 2
2
3
# A NULL column (type ANY) is compatible with any operand's type.
-STATEMENT RETURN 1 AS x UNION ALL RETURN null AS x
---- 2
1

# UNION composing with WITH pipelines in the operands.
-STATEMENT UNWIND [1,2,3] AS x WITH x WHERE x > 1 RETURN x AS v UNION MATCH (n:N) RETURN n.id AS v
---- 3
1
2
3

-CASE UnionValidations
-STATEMENT CREATE NODE TABLE N(id INT64, name STRING, PRIMARY KEY(id))
---- ok
# Different number of columns.
-STATEMENT MATCH (n:N) RETURN n.id, n.name UNION ALL MATCH (m:N) RETURN m.id
---- error
Binder exception: The number of columns to union/union all must be the same.
# Mismatched column types (positional; the offending operand + expected type).
-STATEMENT MATCH (n:N) RETURN n.name UNION ALL MATCH (m:N) RETURN m.id
---- error
Binder exception: m.id has data type INT64 but STRING was expected.
# Mixing UNION and UNION ALL in one query is forbidden.
-STATEMENT MATCH (n:N) RETURN n.id UNION ALL MATCH (m:N) RETURN m.id UNION MATCH (p:N) RETURN p.id
---- error
Binder exception: Union and union all can not be used together.
